            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.224,
                0.208,
                0.773,
                0.239
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 7.28: A load being lifted up (a) vertically, (b) along an inclined plane, and (c) along an inclined plane of larger length"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.242,
            0.888,
            0.278
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "An "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "inclined plane",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a simple machine that helps move a heavy load to a higher (or lower) level. Let us now find its mechanical advantage."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.056,
            0.368,
            0.179,
            0.601
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The work done, that is the product of force and displacement, is the same in all cases. If the force decreases, the displacement increases, thereby the work done remains constant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.28,
            0.889,
            0.349
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let the mass of the object be "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "m"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Then, the load is the weight mg of the object to be lifted. Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "F ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " be the force required to raise the object to a height h (Fig. 7.28a). Then, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "F ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is the effort. Let the length of the inclined plane be L (Fig. 7.28b)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.062,
            0.35,
            0.121,
            0.366
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.35,
            0.889,
            0.385
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If you move the object at constant speed up the inclined plane, then using Eq. (7.2),"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.355,
            0.384,
            0.759,
            0.403
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "total work done by you on the object "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "= F ^ { \\prime } \\times L"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.405,
            0.401,
            0.424
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "And using Eq. (7.8),"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.358,
            0.424,
            0.755,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "potential energy gained by the object = mgh"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.444,
            0.888,
            0.464
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, from the work-energy theorem (Eq. 7.3), we obtain (ignoring friction)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.496,
            0.465,
            0.619,
            0.483
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "F^{\\prime} \\times L = m g h"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.496,
            0.485,
            0.615,
            0.519
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{mg}{F^{\\prime}} = \\frac{L}{h}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.521,
            0.835,
            0.54
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, mg is the load and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "F ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is the effort, so using Eq. (7.12), we obtain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.337,
            0.541,
            0.887,
            0.578
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{mechanism\\;advantage} = \\frac{\\mathrm{l\\;oad}}{\\mathrm{effort}} = \\frac{mg}{F'} = \\frac{L}{h}\\tag{7.13}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.582,
            0.89,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since L is larger than "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "h ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the force "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "F ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is less than mg and the mechanical advantage of inclined plane is greater than 1. By further increasing "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "L ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for example, by making the inclined plane longer with a shallower angle (Fig. 7.28c), we can further reduce the effort "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "F ^ { \\prime }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " required to move the object."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.045,
            0.661,
            0.215,
            0.764
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 18,
              "bbox": [
                0.045,
                0.661,
                0.215,
                0.764
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_16_image_18.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.654,
            0.89,
            0.707
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 7.12:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A person uses an inclined ramp to raise an object over a step 30 cm high. The ramp has a width of 40 cm. What is the mechanical advantage of the ramp that helps the person achieve the task?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.708,
            0.889,
            0.745
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Answer:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " As shown in Fig. 7.29, when the height AB is 30 cm and the width BC is 40 cm, the length AC of the ramp is 50 cm (right-angled triangle property)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.252,
            0.746,
            0.787,
            0.783
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using Eq. (7.13),   mechanical advantage "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{L}{h}=\\frac{50\\  cm }{30\\  cm }=1.67"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.244,
            0.783,
            0.307,
            0.814
          ],
          "content": [
            {
